 60MN2c  Phys Rev C 73, 044322 (2006)                                           
 60MN c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), April 27, 2006                        
 60MN c  {+60}Cr isotope produced by fragmentation of {+86}Kr beam              
 60MN2c  at 140 MeV/nucleon hitting a {+9}Be target. The fragments              
 60MN3c  were separated by A1900 fragment separator. The fully-stripped         
 60MN4c  {+60}Cr ions were implanted in a double-sided Si detector              
 60MN5c  (DSSD) which was also a |b detector. Measured (fragment)|b             
 60MN6c  correlations, isotopic half-life, E|g, I|g, |g|g, |b|g coin. The |g    
 60MN7c  rays were detected with a 12-detector segmented Ge detector array.     
 60MN8c  Comparisons with Shell-model calculations                              
 60MN cB IB,LOGFT$2006Li15 state that |b feeding intensities should be          
 60MN2cB considered as upper limits and associated apparent log| {Ift} values as
 60MN3cB lower limits                                                           
